dsh: reasoning:
Critical bug: `onMounted` in target page: `transfer.peek()` returns pending but never calls `consume()`. So pending stays in memory forever. Also, the tool's onMounted runs when navigating; but the pending payload persists. `peek` doesn't clear. So:
1. Going to a target tool: onMounted peeks, applies... but never consumes. So if you navigate away and back, it will re-apply again (stale pending). Also if you open a *different* target later, old payload still there → unintended transfer. That's a real bug (state leak). Actually deliver() does router.push; consume never called. `consume()` is defined but never used anywhere (grep confirmed only definition). So memory payload never cleared → repeated re-application.

Let me verify by grepping consume( usage again: only useTransfer.ts:45. Yes, never called. Bug.

2. The `onMounted` in t01 checks `input.value.trim()` — but input starts empty on fresh navigation, unless the tool page is kept alive. So replaceAsk only triggers if input already had content. But since route navigation within same component? Nuxt page for /tools/[slug] — the page component is `tools/[slug].vue` which likely renders different components dynamically. Going from one tool to another may reuse... Actually replaceAsk check at mount time: input is empty always at mount (fresh component). So the "替换确认" (replace confirmation) basically never triggers in practice, because receiving tool component is mounted fresh with empty input. Let me verify the architecture: `pages/tools/[slug].vue`.

